Both hold the same data; a class also fixes which fields exist and can carry the functions that use them.

class Price:
    def __init__(self, euros):
        self.cents = round(euros * 100)   # stored differently

    def euros(self):
        return self.cents / 100

print(Price(2.5).euros())   # 2.5
Callers only use Price(...) and .euros(), so the class may change how it stores the value. This is data abstraction.

